{"module name":"neorv32_cpu_control","module purpose":"neorv32_cpu_control is the CPU control-state machine: it accepts fetched instructions, tracks execution state and control-flow addresses, decodes ALU/LSU/register-file/CSR control on ctrl_o, manages machine/debug/trigger CSRs, and detects, prioritizes, and sequences traps, interrupts, sleep, and debug mode. It also returns CSR read data on csr_rdata_o.","use-case flows":[{"flow":"operate","value":"accept a fetched instruction, latch instruction context, and advance execution state and PC","lines":[275,276,358,360,364,365,367,368,369,370]},{"flow":"operate","value":"decode the current instruction into immediate, ALU, LSU, register-writeback, fence, and CSR control outputs","lines":[220,221,222,224,227,229,231,233,235,239,281,316,323,331,339,342,351,404,421,433,442,445,472,475,483,488,504,530,540,577,585,591,601,608,610,611,615,617]},{"flow":"configure","value":"write machine, privilege, interrupt, debug, and trigger CSR state","lines":[1050,1051,1059,1062,1105,1117,1128,1136,1141,1151,1156,1164,1188,1198,1206,1215,1222]},{"flow":"operate","value":"detect, buffer, prioritize, and enter or exit exception, interrupt, and debug handling","lines":[358,359,373,375,380,387,388,392,394,399,835,849,854,867,877,888,899,911,912,919,926,936,971,978,979,983,997,1000,1007,1012,1231,1260,1269]},{"flow":"read out","value":"return selected internal or external CSR contents on csr_rdata_o","lines":[1361,1363,1371,1418,1439,1446,1455,1531,1539,1595]},{"flow":"report","value":"export execution control and status on ctrl_o","lines":[577,578,579,581,582,583,585,591,601,606,608,610,611,613,619,620,621,622]},{"flow":"reset","value":"initialize execution state, trap state, CSR state, debug state, and trigger state","lines":[266,267,268,269,270,271,272,273,633,837,838,839,840,921,922,973,974,975,1022,1023,1047,1048,1072,1073,1074,1075,1084,1098,1100,1357,1358,1359,1630,1631,1701,1702]}],"conceptual assets":[{"concept":"Fetched instruction